# Build context exclusions for BOTH images (the root context feeds the API
# image — ./Dockerfile — and the frontend image when Render builds it without
# an explicit dockerContext).
#
# IMPORTANT (observed): Docker anchors a pattern that contains no `/` to the
# WHOLE relative path, so a bare `.env.*` does NOT match `frontend/.env.local`.
# Nested paths therefore need an explicit `**/` prefix.
#
# Rule of thumb: anything the image rebuilds (`yarn build`) or creates at
# runtime must never be sent as context.

# ── Dependencies: installed inside the image with `yarn install --frozen-lockfile`
node_modules
**/node_modules

# ── Build output: always regenerated inside the image
**/dist
**/.next
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report

# ── Test sources + throwaway test database (production images never run tests)
backend/test

# ── Secrets / local env files: no .env may ever reach an image layer
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.env.local

# ── Databases: SQLite is runtime state on the /app/data disk, never baked in
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite

# ── Repo docs & screenshots: the API image only `COPY backend/`, so nothing
# here is ever read by a build. They are 90 MB of the context (measured:
# docs/ 84 MB, design-preview/ 5.9 MB, screenshots/ 2.4 MB) and Render uploads
# the whole context on EVERY deploy — excluding them keeps the API build fast.
docs
screenshots
design-preview

# ── Local noise
.git
.gitignore
**/*.md
**/*.log
**/.tmp
